## Purpose of Function:                                                              #
##   HTTP-triggered Azure Function exposing ONE endpoint with TWO modes, selected     #
##   by the 'agent' field in the request:                                             #
##                                                                                    #
##     agent = 'detect'    -> return ONLY the detected language of 'message'          #
##                            [LLM-based; py3langid offline fallback].                #
##     agent = 'translate' -> translate 'message' into the target 'lang' using the    #
##                            Azure OpenAI model.                                      #
##                                                                                    #
## Request contract (query string OR JSON body):                                      #
##     agent    : 'detect' | 'translate'                    [required]                #
##     message  : text to detect / translate                [required]                #
##     lang     : target language for 'translate'           [required for translate]  #
##                (ISO code 'ja', alias 'jp' or name 'Japanese')                      #
##                                                                                    #
## WHAT CHANGED (direct LLM call instead of the named agent):                          #
##   Previously each request cost TWO upstream round-trips - conversations.create()    #
##   then responses.create() with an agent_reference - plus a server-side agent        #
##   lookup on every call. The agent's system prompt now lives in this file            #
##   (AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT) and the model is called directly over Chat Completions:     #
##   ONE round-trip, no agent resolution, no conversation object.                      #
##   The request/response contract is UNCHANGED - callers need no modification.        #
##                                                                                    #
## MODEL NOTE (gpt-5-mini is a REASONING model):                                       #
##   It requires 'max_completion_tokens' (not 'max_tokens'), rejects any non-default   #
##   'temperature', and supports 'reasoning_effort' (set to 'minimal' because both     #
##   modes are short mechanical tasks). Reasoning tokens count against the output      #
##   ceiling, which is why DETECT_MAX_TOKENS is 512 and not 8 - a tiny ceiling can be  #
##   consumed entirely by reasoning and return an EMPTY reply. If the deployment is    #
##   ever swapped to a gpt-4o family model, _chat() detects the rejected parameters    #
##   and switches to the legacy dialect once per worker.                               #
##                                                                                    #
## Production hardening applied:                                                       #
##   * LLM client + credential built ONCE and reused across requests (cached).         #
##   * Per-call timeout + automatic retries on the LLM calls.                          #
##   * Bounded input length (MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS) to protect cost / prevent abuse.       #
##   * Bounded output ceiling + minimal reasoning effort so replies stay fast.         #
##   * Only the first DETECT_SAMPLE_CHARS characters are sent for detection.           #
##   * No internal exception detail leaked to callers; full detail logged instead.     #
##   * correlation_id on EVERY response and injected into EVERY log record.            #
##   * Structured logs (extra=...) with latency + engine ('foundry' | 'offline').      #
##                                                                                    #
## Authentication:                                                                     #
##   The Azure OpenAI endpoint is reached with Microsoft Entra ID (no API keys). The   #
##   Function App's Managed Identity MUST live in the SAME tenant as the Azure OpenAI  #
##   resource and hold 'Cognitive Services OpenAI User' on it. NOTE: this is a         #
##   DIFFERENT token audience from the old Foundry 'projects' endpoint - the scope is  #
##   https://cognitiveservices.azure.com/.default                                      #
##                                                                                    #
## Tunable App Settings (all optional, safe defaults in code):                         #
##   AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT, AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT, AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION,         #
##   ENVIRONMENT, MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS, FOUNDRY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS, FOUNDRY_MAX_RETRIES,     #
##   LLM_PARAM_STYLE, LLM_REASONING_EFFORT, LLM_TEMPERATURE, DETECT_MAX_TOKENS,        #
##   TRANSLATE_MAX_TOKENS, DETECT_SAMPLE_CHARS, LOG_LEVEL.                             #
##   No longer read: FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT, FOUNDRY_AGENT_NAME (they only existed to        #
##   resolve the named agent). Leaving them set is harmless.                           #
